  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of proceeds All of the ADSs offered\n    by the selling shareholders pursuant to this prospectus will be sold by the selling shareholders. We will not receive any proceeds\n    from such sales. However, to the extent the Warrants are exercised for cash, if at all, we will receive the exercise prices of those\n    warrants. The exercise prices of the Series A-1 Warrants and Placement Agent Warrants may exceed the trading price of the ADSs. If\n    the price of the ADSs is below the exercise prices of those warrants, we believe that holders of those warrants will be unlikely\n    to exercise them, resulting in little to no cash proceeds to us. If all the Warrants were exercised for cash, we would receive gross\n    proceeds of approximately $6.2 million. See \u201cUse of Proceeds\u201d in this prospectus for more information. Offering price The Pre-Funded Warrants\n    have an exercise price of $0.0001",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk factors You should carefully read\n    the section titled \u201cRisk Factors\u201d and other information included in this prospectus for a discussion of factors that\n    you should consider before deciding to invest in our securities. (1) The number of ADSs to be\n    outstanding immediately after the offering, as shown above, is based on 2,630,416\u00a0ADSs (representing 105,216,880,000 Ordinary\n    Shares) issued and outstanding as of October 21, 2026. As\nof June 30, 2026, we had issued and outstanding warrants to purchase 1,145,022 ADSs, with the expiration dates of these warrants ranging\nfrom 2027 to 2031, and pre-funded warrants to purchase an aggregate of 357,253 ADSs at an exercise price of $0.001. As of such date,\nunder the 2018 Israel Share Option Plan, we also had issued and outstanding options to purchase an aggregate of 12,192 ADSs with the\nrange of expiration dates being between the yea",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
